 "_about": "(polish1 D4c) The TREETOP VILLAGE on the four ring islands (core/treetop_rules.gd, game/treetops.gd). Each village hangs on one giant tree of its island (`tree` = that tree's spot in data/archipelago.json features, island-local metres) and a few platforms on stilts. `layers` = deck heights over the ground (m) for layer 1-3. `rings` = how far a ring deck round the trunk reaches from the trunk's middle per layer (a ladder up from a ring hangs over the ring below with room to stand behind it, so they shrink). A deck: `on` tree (a ring round the trunk at its layer) or stilts (`at` island-local, `size` m, `hut` a thatched hut on it). A WAY is bought like a door, in any order (director): `kind` ladder (climbed, from the ground or the deck below), lift (a basket ride from the ground), bridge (a rope bridge between two decks of the same layer); `from` / `to` deck ids (ground = the island floor), `price` points. Ways are bought for everybody (online the host checks the buyer stands at one end) and reset when the run ends.",
